<title>UK: New Jersey prices multi-tranche dollar bond.</title>
<headline>New Jersey prices multi-tranche dollar bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State of New Jersey has priced a multi-tranche bond for a total of $2.8 billion, lead manager Merrill Lynch said.</p>
<p>The $1.3 billion fixed-rate tranche, which has a legal maturity of February 15, 2029 and an average life of 29.87 years, will pay a 7.425 percent semi-annual coupon. Issue and reoffer price is par. Launch spread is 66 basis points over the 6.5 percent November 2026 U.S. Treasury bond.  </p>
<p>There are also 28 zero-coupon bonds totalling $1.5 billion. These have consecutive maturities from one year to 29 years, but excluding a two-year bond.</p>
